WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:02.740
"And I know you, 'cause
you're from my hometown."

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:04.400
"Richard Ramirez."

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:05.940
"Night Stalker."

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.280
"You just died of cancer
in your cell a few years back."

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:10.680
"So that was a f*king lie."

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.540
Bertie's back, bitches, and she
wants to play some strip pictionary.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.660
Yes, another season of "American
Horror Story" has come, it's so sad,

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.980
and Think Story is here to
break down the final episode,

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.160
and I gotta say, I really enjoyed this season.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.580
I know the campiness - get
it? - isn't everyone's cup of tea,

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.320
but overall, I gotta rank
this in my Top 3 Seasons.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.560
That being said, don't
form a mob or anything,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.280
but the final episode for me left
a lot of unanswered questions.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:45.080
And there were some character arcs that weren't
fully fleshed out and lots of plot inconsistencies,

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:50.340
so I may do one of my "How it should have ended"-
videos if I have time in the upcoming days.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.980
If you haven't seen the one I did
for last season's "Apocalypse",

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.940
I've left a link in the description below.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.860
We are back at Camp
Redwood, this time in 2019.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.740
An Uber drives Bobby Richter,

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.700
yes, the now adult son of Mr. Jingles,

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:08.260
to the abandoned camp, which hasn't been
touched since that ill-fated Fyre Festiv-,

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:11.920
I mean, Camp Redwood
Festival back in 1989.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:17.000
Bobby passes a rusted wood chipper,
foreshadowing the kickass gore that's to come,

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.480
We can see by the entrance sign:
This place has seen better days.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.580
And even the stage hasn't been touched.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:26.240
I'm still a little bitter we didn't
get to see Evan Peters as Billy Idol.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:31.360
Bobby takes pictures with his cell phone when
Montana appears, who asks him what that device is.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:36.540
No one has really visited the place since '89,
so she wouldn't know what a cellphone is.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.940
When he tells her he's the son of
Jingles who's come looking for answers,

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:40.980
she gives him a hug.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.160
As we'll find out, Montana has turned a new leaf.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.500
Killing isn't her priority,
at least not anymore.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:49.460
Just be careful what
you say around her, Bobby.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.040
What did you say?

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.540
Taking Bobby to the cabin,
we also see that Trevor's there.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:00.260
He has survived his tragic dick
shooting, which we'll get to in a bit.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:05.280
Bobby has a scrapbook filled with information
about the camp, including all of its victims.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:10.140
He tells Montana that his aunt on her
deathbed told him the truth about his father.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:15.360
That's why he's now all of a sudden ventured to
the camp in search of answers 30 years later.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:19.820
He's also the luckiest person on the planet,
receiving anonymous checks from someone,

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.840
and wants to find out who sent them.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:25.540
Unfortunately for Bobby, the
ghost of Jingles hasn't been seen,

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:31.340
Montana saying that she saw with her own
eyes him being taken away by dark forces.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:36.520
She's referring to him being thrown overboard
by the drowned, deformed corpse of his brother,

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:42.000
the one he was supposed to be looking after, but instead was perving some counselors making sexy time.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:46.100
Montana grabs Bobby's gun from his backpack
to prove that she can come back to life,

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.940
that's like a great party trick,

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:51.060
when we're transported back to 1989.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:54.520
Margaret is pissed, because the
talent is nowhere to be found.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.160
She's chilling with Ricky and Bruce,

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.560
and when Courtney comes in telling
her that Trevor has blocked the road,

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.060
she shoots him in the face.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:04.240
So disrespectful after he
cleaned up that entire tour bus.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.840
And I think the only thing more offensive
than Trevor's shirt is this dude's troll hair.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:14.460
At the entrance to Redwood, Trevor has slashed the
tires of what appears to be Kajagoogoo's tour bus.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:20.240
He's done with putting up with Margaret's crap and proclaims to his wife his undying love for Montana.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.360
But Margaret won't let him get away with this.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.940
She shoots him not just in
the chest, but in the dick.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.500
"That's got to hurt. I don't
care where you're from."

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:32.100
And if getting shot in the dick wasn't terrifying
enough, he was shot over the property line,

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:35.500
meaning if he dies, he won't
resurrect as one of the ghosts.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:38.500
Montana appears, but she, too, is helpless.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.700
She can't cross the line to save him,

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.140
but it's Brooke who comes to save the day.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.900
She's turned a new leaf after
almost killing the journalist last episode,

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:50.480
and has embraced the good
side, helping Trevor over the line.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:51.620
Back in present day,

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:55.120
Montana catches Bobby up to speed
on what happened to Margaret, Bruce,

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:58.500
and of course, the Night
Stalker himself, Ricky Ramirez.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:01.720
The ghosts ended up banding
together to put a stop to them,

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:08.340
even using Midge, this character here who you might remember as one of the original 1970 massacre victims,

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:10.480
as a decoy to kill Bruce.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.820
I also love how he holds the
knife here, 'cause he has no thumbs.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:19.560
Trevor stabs Bruce and kicks him outside the
bounds of the property, so he won't be able to resurrect.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:21.880
Ramirez, however, is a different story.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:24.420
They just can't kill him and
chuck him off the property,

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:28.700
because he'll just resurrect by the
power of Satan and go off to kill Bobby.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.760
Montana's plan is to
set up a death watch,

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:43.480
lure Ramirez into Lavinia's shack and repeatedly murder him every time he resurrects until the end of time.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.480
I mean, I guess the
alternative was to let him go,

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:50.680
but since Montana says there are tons
of ghosts there, they can take turns.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:52.400
Xavier uses a chainsaw,

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:57.280
and Ray even unleashes his inner Annie Wilkes
by hobbling his legs with a sledgehammer.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:59.020
- "It's for the best."
- "Annie, please!"

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:04.440
And I will say Ramirez' death is probably
the goriest death we've seen in ages to date.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:07.300
Like, I'll get demonetised
if I even try to show it.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.420
As Montana says, the ghosts
took up Mr. Jingles' mantle,

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:14.020
protecting Bobby in the world
from the evil that is Ricky Ramirez.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:19.620
We then are sent 20 minutes earlier, where Bertie
puts the moves on Chet, leaving Ricky unattended.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:23.300
But the thing that's even more far-fetched
than this scenario is the fact that

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:28.740
tonight of all nights, Ricky
escapes not just once, but twice.

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:33.940
After 30 years, Ricky attacks Bobby by
throwing this huge ass knife into his back.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:34.720
I mean look at it.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.640
And I love how he just kind of forgets

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.800
he has a giant, life-threatening gash in
his back the next few scenes at the asylum.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:46.200
Ricky really wants to kill Bobby as payment for
his dad's betrayal of both himself and Satan,

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:48.220
saying that he needs to pay his debt.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:53.480
But Bobby is saved yet again by the ghosts and told
by Montana to go to the Red Meadows Asylum.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:57.880
Now, this is also the last we see Ricky,
which was kind of a letdown for me.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:01.980
I, I guess we're to assume that the ghosts
once again continued their death watch?

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:03.860
Uh-oh, guys, who's on death watch?

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:05.400
Bobby arrives at Red Meadows,

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:09.940
the same hospital where his father was kept
and had been subjected to electroshock therapy.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.120
Bobby strolls in looking like a hobo

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:16.620
and just expects to speak to the director
at what is probably 11 o'clock at night.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:18.840
Bobby, how do you think
this is gonna go down?

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:22.460
Then these orderlies come in and
take him away, which I think is illegal,

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:23.960
but whatever, I'm here for it.

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:26.120
When he mentions his father's name,

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:30.380
a name which Donna Chambers,
the now medical director, recognizes,

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:32.500
it's kind of ironic that she's the director,

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:38.460
since she was the one who orchestrated Jingles'
escape from that very institution way back in '84.

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:42.160
She tells him Margaret was the
real killer and recounts her story.

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:45.780
The angry mob of ghosts have surrounded
the cabin while Margaret loads her gun.

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:49.360
But it's Donna who's the first
to take a stab at her - literally.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:52.120
Brooke comes to save the
day, but in the scuffle is shot.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:53.760
We'll get back to her in a second.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:58.680
Margaret is brought out to the wood chipper where
her limbs are systematically cut off one by one.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:00.620
"I'm already dying."

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:02.780
"Right, we'll call it a draw."

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:07.660
It's only fitting that Trevor gets to call the shots here
as revenge for his elephant truck getting shot.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.300
And he friggin' Kobe's
her head into the chipper.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:13.440
Now, it's really easy to miss,
because it happens really fast,

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:18.360
but when her head, which Montana says can
live 30 seconds after being decapitated,

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:19.980
is thrown into the chipper,

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:23.540
the wind blows her guts back
onto the Redwood property,

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:26.300
which is why I guess
she was able to resurrect.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:30.820
Donna tells Bobby that she was the
final girl, that Brooke died that night,

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:34.380
but if Donna wasn't the one
sending him checks, who was it?

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:38.660
They're able to locate the post office by
tracing the routing number found on the checks,

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:40.660
which leads them all the way to Oregon.

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:43.100
It's there they find Brooke is still alive.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:47.340
Not only that but she has her
own family, her own normal life.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:51.000
Now, Emma Roberts is supposed
to be like, 50, 60 years old here,

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:55.820
and I love how they try to brush off that she doesn't
look old by saying her husband is a dermatologist.

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:56.540
Okay.

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:58.860
Donna is upset and for good reason:

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:03.800
she's carried this guilt with her for 30 years
that she was responsible for Brooke's death.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:09.000
And I gotta be honest, Brooke's response that
it was just too hard for her was kind of weak.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.780
We find out that Ray was the
one who helped Brooke out.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.940
The bullet went right through her
and says he'll get some bandages.

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:17.780
Ray, you're probably gonna need a lot
more than bandages for this one.

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:22.020
However, I forgive it because they do
this cute iodine and bandage throwback,

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:26.620
which is a nod to their first somewhat
romantic encounter back in episode 1.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:32.160
Ray leads her to the edge of the property and all she remembers is passing out and waking up in a hospital.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:36.000
And somehow the tour bus that was
blocking the way has magically been removed.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:40.120
Brooke sent checks to Bobby as her
way of coping with what had happened.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:43.800
She said she needed a glimmer
of hope in all the darkness.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:47.200
She had seen that a once evil
man could find redemption,

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:50.660
turn his life around and start
a family and be a good person.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:54.580
She also knows how Camp Redwood
has a way of pulling people back.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:59.560
Perhaps if Bobby was given money,
he could break free from this "awful legacy".

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:03.560
Brooke and Donna turn out to be
the final girls and I gotta be honest,

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:05.720
I thought Brooke's ending was pretty weak,

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:10.140
considering they built her up to be probably
the closest to a main character this season.

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:12.680
But let me know what you guys
think in the comments below.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:16.620
Outside Brooke's, Bobby tells Donna
that he has to go back to Redwood,

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.800
that he felt something when he was there.

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:23.580
I guess Brooke was right that the camp really
does have a way of pulling people back in.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:27.920
It's at Redwood that Bobby meets Margaret,
who survived her trip to the wood chipper.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:31.080
She says she's the only one
who knows where his father is.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:35.540
How she knows this is never explained.
Maybe she's lying, I don' know.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:41.240
And later when Jingles appears before Bobby, we
never get a clear answer how he magically shows up.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:45.360
This to me is one of the more
frustrating aspects of the season:

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:50.320
the rules surrounding the whole curse and
resurrection stuff is conveniently twisted,

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:54.680
so that the writers can adjust it to fit
whatever plot point they're trying to achieve.

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:58.420
For example, in some episodes the
bodies take time before they're resurrected,

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:01.300
and in others they magically
appear moments later.

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:05.040
Jingles isn't able to be found for
30 years, but then comes out at the end.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:07.640
Where was he when Bobby first arrived?

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:09.580
Where was Jingles this whole time?

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:14.600
Somewhere at the camp or in his own personal
heaven, as I theorized in my episode 8 video?

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:20.100
All of this is very muddy, but I still liked how Bobby
was able to finally meet his dad and grandma.

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:21.240
(Chorus) Aww!

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.700
Jingles asks Jingles, jr. why he came back,

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:27.040
and he says it was to thank him
for the sacrifice his father made,

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:31.280
so that he could grow up and be free
without the specter of Ricky after him.

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:34.280
Lavinia is the one to kill
Margaret, which is kind of ironic,

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:39.500
since Lavinia was the first massacre perpetrator
killing Margaret, who's the second and third.

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:45.720
The ghosts say farewell to Bobby and Montana talks about how the 80s will never die, just like themselves.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:51.860
With the final scene taking place between Bobby and
his family, his grandmother, father, and uncle Bobby.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:55.240
I'll get more into this if I end up doing a
"How it should have ended"-video,

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:59.680
but the thing that disappointed me the
most was the lack of closure for the ghosts,

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:03.940
specifically a few of them who had cool
backstories and traumas that were explored,

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:06.640
yet their redemptive arcs
were never really panned out.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:10.680
I would also have loved to have seen more
lore behind the curse surrounding the camp

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:12.880
and tie-ins to other seasons.

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:18.840
I think they missed a valuable opportunity to tie Ricky in with Michael Langdon and last season's "Apocalypse".

00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:22.360
They have so many similarities,
yet that was all glossed over.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.100
Overall, though, this
season was fun as hell.

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:27.660
I don't think there was a
dud episode in the bunch.

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:30.960
As much as I throw shade at
the show, I do it out of love.

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:34.240
So I hope you'll consider stabbing
that like button, subscribing,

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:36.960
and leaving a comment about
what you thought about the season.

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:40.080
You can also follow me
on Twitter @ThinkStoryYT.

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:42.040
Until next season remember,

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:43.580
Daddy loves you very much.

